{:name "mcp"
 :version "1.0.0"
 :description "Optional MCP endpoint package — the JSON-RPC 2.0 `/mcp` tool surface an external AI drives (fn-def sync, execute, branch/diff, graph read). Extracted from `app` so a deployment that does not want to expose an AI endpoint can omit `\"mcp\"` from :package-names and the app still boots; its route is served per-branch through the branch-router's optional-handler slot (`_mcp-ring-response`, wired in `:exec/branch-router`), so `app` no longer references it."
 ;; Sits ABOVE `app`: the MCP tools compose app's execution / branch /
 ;; lookup fn-defs (`:fn-id-by-name`, `:resolve-branch-ref`, `:_execute-*`,
 ;; `:_create-branch-*`), plus the `app-base` auth route template `:post`.
 ;; `app` does NOT depend on `mcp` (the `:mcp-route` ref was removed from
 ;; app's `:all`), so the edge is one-way and dropping `mcp` is safe.
 ;; The fn `:namespace` stays `app.mcp` — identity is
 ;; uuid-v5(namespace,name), so moving only the directory leaves every id
 ;; + ref byte-identical. The module has no impls: every tool is
 ;; composition over base-fns other packages ship.
 :dependencies ["core" "web" "app"]
 :modules ["mcp"]}
